## 5. Benefits Demonstrated
- Automated creation of laptop configuration tasks.
- Consistent assignment of tasks to the Hardware group.
- Reduced need for manual task creation.
- Improved visibility into the laptop request process.
- More structured handling of standard laptop procurement requests.

## 6. Conclusion
The project demonstration presents the end-to-end workflow for automating standard laptop procurement using ServiceNow Flow Designer. It covers flow configuration, catalog item association, request submission, approval, and verification of the generated catalog task. The demonstration is intended to show how workflow automation can improve task assignment and reduce manual effort in IT procurement.

The final demonstration should confirm that the flow creates the task at the intended approval stage and that the generated catalog task contains the required details.
